Quoted documentation
--------------------

issuers.yaml, issuers.json, and the copy of issuers.json in the Python package
quote vendors' public documentation. The quoted words are their publishers'
text: the Apache License above covers this project's own work and does not
relicense them.

The tenancy facts quote sentences verbatim, each beside the URL of the page it
was read on and the date it was read. The entry fields aud_evidence,
vendor_example, vendor_example_note and self_hosted_variant quote shorter
passages and the vendors' example policies, naming the vendor; not every one
carries the page's URL and the date it was read.

Where a publisher states a licence for the pages quoted, it is recorded here as
read on 2026-09-27:

- docs.github.com (GitHub Docs): Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International, per the LICENSE of https://github.com/github/docs.
- kubernetes.io (Kubernetes documentation, The Kubernetes Authors): Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International, per the LICENSE of
  https://github.com/kubernetes/website and the pages' footer.
- cloud.google.com/docs, docs.cloud.google.com and developers.google.com
  (Google): the pages quoted say "Except as otherwise noted, the content of
  this page is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License,
  and code samples are licensed under the Apache 2.0 License."
- learn.microsoft.com (Microsoft): the Azure Kubernetes Service pages are
  published from https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/azure-aks-docs, whose
  LICENSE is Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International; the Microsoft
  Entra pages are published from https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs,
